alias ExitStatus = std::process::ExitStatus;
alias Inputs = std::process::Inputs;

public fn run(inputs: Inputs) -> status: ExitStatus pure waits doc "The html_tree_oracle entry, invoked as `html_tree_oracle PATH` with PATH naming the case file that tests/html/tree_oracle.py writes, relative to the working directory: per case, a header line `SCRIPTING CONTEXT_LENGTH INPUT_LENGTH` in decimal with SCRIPTING 0 or 1, the fragment context's bytes, the input's bytes and a line feed. An empty context makes the case a document, parsed by parse_document; otherwise the context is `svg NAME` for an SVG context element, `math NAME` for a MathML one, or NAME alone for an HTML one, NAME being a nonempty local name without spaces, and the case is parsed by parse_fragment with NAME interned. All cases share one atom table. For every case it prints the parsed document's tree as serialize_document writes it, the root's children at depth 0, and then a line `#end`. When the walk of the tree stops at inconsistent links it adds the line `| driver: tree links are inconsistent` before `#end`; when parsing fails it prints the line `| driver: parse failed (TooLarge)`, or `(Dom InvalidNode)`, `(Dom WrongKind)` or `(Dom TooLarge)` for a document operation's refusal, instead of a tree; and when atom_intern refuses the context name it prints `| driver: atom_intern refused the context name (TooLarge)` without parsing. Every such line differs from every expected tree. It exits with 0 after printing every case, and with 2, after the cases before it and a message on standard error, when it is not given exactly one argument or the case file cannot be read or is malformed.";
